// Ed25519 public keys a contract must not accept as an independent authority:
// small-order points and non-canonical encodings, prohibited as a set.
//
// Tol counterpart of crypto/smartcont/strong-ed25519-key.fc, with the same
// keys read the same way: the 256-bit integer `loadUint(256)` produces from
// the 32 encoded bytes. For a key in the 8-torsion subgroup a signature can be
// forged with no secret; this repository's tests demonstrate it for the
// identity and order-2 point with the sign bit set and for the canonical
// order-2 point. Not every encoding below takes a forgery (the VM's signature
// check itself refuses the all-zero key and the canonical identity), but all
// are refused regardless. A contract that counts a stored key's signature
// toward an authorization must refuse them, or whoever configured the key can
// name one nobody needs a secret for.
//
// Refused:
//   - the eight canonical encodings of the torsion subgroup;
//   - the identity (y = 1) and the order-2 point (y = -1) with the sign bit
//     set. Both have x = 0, so the sign bit names no other point: these are
//     non-canonical aliases of the same two points, and their y is in range;
//   - every encoding whose y is at least 2^255 - 19, with either sign bit.
// The other torsion points have x != 0, so flipping their sign bit gives
// another canonical torsion encoding already listed. Callers throw their own
// error code.
tol 1.3

// Grouped by first byte, as in strong-ed25519-key.fc: below 0xec the listed
// encodings come in pairs that differ only in the sign bit, so one comparison
// with that bit forced on covers both; 0xec..0xff share one test, bytes 1..30
// all 0xff and y's top byte 0x7f with either sign bit (the order-2 point and
// its alias at 0xec, every y >= 2^255 - 19 above it).

/// True for every key [ed25519IsWeakKey] refuses. A few instructions, so a
/// caller short of gas can skip the full check for almost every real key.
fun ed25519KeyMayBeWeak(publicKey: int): bool {
    val first = publicKey >> 248;
    return first <= 0x01 || first == 0x26 || first == 0xc7 || first >= 0xec;
}

fun ed25519IsWeakKey(publicKey: int): bool {
    if ((publicKey >> 248) >= 0xec) {
        return ((publicKey >> 8) & ((1 << 240) - 1)) == ((1 << 240) - 1) && (publicKey & 127) == 127;
    }
    val eitherSign = publicKey | 0x80;
    return eitherSign == 0x80
        || eitherSign == 0x0100000000000000000000000000000000000000000000000000000000000080
        || eitherSign == 0x26e8958fc2b227b045c3f489f2ef98f0d5dfac05d3c63339b13802886d53fc85
        || eitherSign == 0xc7176a703d4dd84fba3c0b760d10670f2a2053fa2c39ccc64ec7fd7792ac03fa;
}
